          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c2_classic_approaches_require_projectin",
          "text": "The classic approaches require projecting onto the semidefinite cone, which needs a full eigendecomposition that scales cubically with problem size.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "classic",
            "approaches",
            "require",
            "projecting",
            "onto",
            "semidefinite",
            "cone",
            "which",
            "needs",
            "full"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c3_recent_sketching_methods_like_cgal",
          "text": "Recent sketching methods, like CGAL, avoid storing the full matrix and scale much further, but they pay for it: as the problem grows they need more and more iterations, so convergence slows down.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "recent",
            "sketching",
            "methods",
            "like",
            "cgal",
            "avoid",
            "storing",
            "full",
            "matrix",
            "scale"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s02_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s02_c4_worse_they_rely_iteration_dependent",
          "text": "Worse, they rely on iteration-dependent parameter schedules that prevent them from reliably reusing a previous solution as a warm start, which is exactly what many real applications need.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "worse",
            "they",
