        {
          "chunk_index": 2,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c02",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c2_all_these_settings_new_problem",
          "text": "In all these settings, each new problem is nearly identical to the last, so being able to warm-start from the previous solution should give a huge speedup.",
          "expected_role": "content",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "all",
            "these",
            "settings",
            "new",
            "problem",
            "nearly",
            "identical",
            "last",
            "being",
            "able"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 3,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c03",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c3_spectral_bundle_methods_appealing_fr",
          "text": "Spectral bundle methods are an appealing framework here: they have low per-iteration cost and fast empirical convergence.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "spectral",
            "bundle",
            "methods",
            "appealing",
            "framework",
            "they",
            "low",
            "per-iteration",
            "cost",
            "fast"
          ],
          "required": true
        },
        {
          "chunk_index": 4,
          "chunk_id": "s03_c04",
          "anchor_id": "cue_s03_c4_but_previous_spectral_bundle_methods",
          "text": "But previous spectral bundle methods handled either only equality constraints or only inequality constraints, and none had an efficient standalone implementation that could be evaluated on truly massive SDPs.",
          "expected_role": "method",
          "cue_keywords": [
            "but",
            "previous",
